comments.body:
@opermajki thanks for the finding and this issue.
The devonfw initiative is IMHO a very great initiative with lots of highlights but to be very honest, this issue on the other hand shows that there are also low-lights. It is a pitty that such an issue exists in devonfw that claims to reduce risks and be a great solution for IT security. If the detailed guides that we have online would have been read and honored, this security and data-privacy desaster would of course not have happened. The actual pain-story however is that we have not been able to make any progress and more or less ignored this issue for 1+ year!
I marked this issue as bug and blocker and will put priority on this so we will get this fixed. Sorry, for this pain-story but shit happenes. Lets try to make the best for the future, keep on going to continuously improve devonfw and my-thai-star and make things like this become history to forget one fine day :)
